## 28 — Find the Index of the First Occurrence in a String

## Approach — Brute Force String Matching

### Idea
We need to find the first position where `needle` appears completely inside `haystack`.
Instead of using Java's built-in `indexOf()`, we check every possible starting position in `haystack`.
For each `start` position:

1. Set `i = start` to point to the current position in `haystack`.
2. Set `j = 0` to start from the beginning of `needle`.
3. Compare both characters while they match.
4. If a mismatch occurs, stop checking that starting position and move to the next `start`.
5. If `j` reaches the length of `needle`, the complete string has been found, so return `start`.
6. If no match is found after checking all starting positions, return `-1`.

### Complexity
Time: O(h × n)
Space: O(1)`

Where:
h = length of `haystack`
n = length of `needle`

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int strStr(String haystack, String needle) {

        int h = haystack.length();
        int n = needle.length();

        for (int start = 0; start < h; start++) {

            int i = start;
            int j = 0;

            while (i < h && j < n &&
                   haystack.charAt(i) == needle.charAt(j)) {
                i++;
                j++;
            }

            if (j == n)
                return start;
        }

        return -1;
    }
}
